BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai-horizons-parma-360-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T165531Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: AI Horizons: Art Beyond Algorithms (PARMA 360 Festival\, 
 Parma European Youth Capital 2027)
DESCRIPTION:First edition of an international call for artists under 35 wor
 king with artificial intelligence\, digital languages and emerging technol
 ogies\, run by 360° Creativity Events APS for PARMA 360 Festival and Parm
 a European Youth Capital 2027. It follows the 2026 pilot exhibition SYNTHE
 TIC HORIZONS (curated by Chiara Canali).\n\nOrganisation: 360° Creativity
  Events APS (PARMA 360 Festival della creatività contemporanea)\, with Pa
 rma European Youth Capital 2027\nLocation: Parma\, Italy. Open to Italian 
 and international artists under 35 and students of the Accademie di Belle 
 Arti. Finalists exhibit in Parma in April-May 2027.\nAward: EUR 6\,000 in 
 cash prizes (gross): 1st AI Horizons Prize EUR 1\,500 (overall winner) plu
 s three sponsor prizes of EUR 1\,500 each (Polo Parma for Parma Heritage\,
  COLSER-Auroradomus for La Cura\, DS Solutions for Sustainability and Data
  Ecology). The top prize can be combined with a sponsor prize\, so one art
 ist can receive up to EUR 3\,000. Prizes are treated as full or partial ac
 quisition of the work. Non-cash: Piazza of Beauty residency in Parma durin
 g the show\, plus Rome New Media Week 2027 and Premio Giovanarte exhibitio
 n mentions. Free to enter.\nDuration: Finalist group exhibition in April-M
 ay 2027 (11th PARMA 360 Festival)\n\nMore: https://forms.gle/ymoWbcjuDyzJY
 11P6?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://forms.gle/ymoWbcjuDyzJY11P6?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Parma\, Italy. Open to Italian and international artists under 35 
 and students of the Accademie di Belle Arti. Finalists exhibit in Parma in
  April-May 2027.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gainssa-ai-safety-essentials-fellowship-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261104T165531Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:Deadline: GAIN SSA: AI Safety Essentials Fellowship (inaugural coho
 rt)
DESCRIPTION:GAIN SSA (Global AI Youth Network\, Sub-Saharan Africa) runs th
 e AI Safety Essentials Fellowship for residents of Africa considering how 
 they can be effective contributors in shaping the continent's transition t
 oward containing risks from transformative AI.\n\nOrganisation: GAIN SSA (
 Global AI Youth Network\, Sub-Saharan Africa)\nLocation: Online (virtual\,
  facilitated). Open to residents of African countries.\nAward: Micro-grant
  pool funding top capstone proposals at USD 500 to 1\,000 each (capped at 
 USD 1\,000)\, usable for compute access\, communication work such as Subst
 ack Pro subscriptions for writers\, or travel to AI alignment conferences 
 in Sub-Saharan Africa. The fellowship itself is free to attend (no partici
 pation fee\, no application fee)\; no stipend is paid during the program.\
 nDuration: 6-week facilitated virtual curriculum plus an onboarding pre-re
 quisites module (the site also describes it as 7 weeks)\, about 5 hours pe
 r week with one live group call per week\; capstone proposals are funded a
 fterwards\, with results within 10 days of submission.\n\nMore: https://ga
 inssa.org/initiatives/fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
URL:https://gainssa.org/initiatives/fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online (virtual\, facilitated). Open to residents of African count
 ries.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:humanity-ai-open-call-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T165531Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Humanity AI: Open Call for Proposals 2026
DESCRIPTION:Humanity AI\, an initiative of ten leading philanthropies\, ope
 ns a USD 10 million call for community-led initiatives that shape how AI a
 ffects people's lives.\n\nOrganisation: Humanity AI (coalition of 10 phila
 nthropies)\nLocation: United States. Lead applicants must be US-based 501(
 c)(3) organizations (or Tribal governments)\; all proposals must serve US-
 based communities. Individuals can apply through a fiscal sponsor or as pa
 rt of a collaboration.\nAward: USD 10 million total pool\, grants of USD 7
 5\,000 to 1\,000\,000 across three tiers: Tier 1 USD 75\,000-150\,000\; Ti
 er 2 USD 150\,000-500\,000\; Tier 3 USD 500\,000-1\,000\,000. Grants run u
 p to three years. No application fee.\nDuration: Up to three years\n\nMore
 : https://humanityai.ai/open-call/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://humanityai.ai/open-call/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:United States. Lead applicants must be US-based 501(c)(3) organiza
 tions (or Tribal governments)\; all proposals must serve US-based communit
 ies. Individuals can apply through a fiscal sponsor or as part of a collab
 oration.
END:VEVENT
