 ety's TICTeC (The Impacts of Civic Technology) series\, run with the AI fo
 r Collective Intelligence (AI4CI) Research Hub\, the Scottish Government a
 nd the Edinburgh Futures Institute\, for researchers\, policy makers and p
 ractitioners reimagining technology for more resilient democracies.\n\nOrg
 anisation: mySociety (TICTeC) with the AI for Collective Intelligence (AI4
 CI) Hub\, the Scottish Government and the Edinburgh Futures Institute\, Un
 iversity of Edinburgh\nLocation: Edinburgh Futures Institute\, Edinburgh\,
  Scotland\, UK. Primarily in-person\, with a limited number of remote pres
 entation slots.\nAward: NO GUARANTEED CASH\, listed as an exception at the
  editor's request: accepted speakers get complimentary conference registra
 tion\, and a limited number of travel scholarships are available for speak
 ers who could otherwise not attend (priority to applicants from ODA-eligib
 le countries and under-29s\; amount not published). Free to submit.\nDurat
 ion: Two-day conference\, 11-12 March 2027.\n\nMore: https://tictec.mysoci
 ety.org/event/digital-democracy-edinburgh/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://tictec.mysociety.org/event/digital-democracy-edinburgh/?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Edinburgh Futures Institute\, Edinburgh\, Scotland\, UK. Primarily
  in-person\, with a limited number of remote presentation slots.
END:VEVENT
